{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"9066ed54e1a6467355e1337f9dbc6b78c195ffb78fd9113fb608533c77feeee4","packTokens":4862,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":4585,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nState, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a person submits a Google OAuth identity, the Folio3 Parking web app shall create an authenticated session only for an active Folio3 employee authenticated through the corporate Google Workspace.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Google OAuth callback contains an active employee identity in the Folio3 corporate Workspace domain when The callback is submitted then The response status is 200 and the response contains an authenticated session field\",\n    \"Given A Google OAuth callback contains a personal Gmail identity, a non-Folio3 identity, or an inactive employee identity when The callback is submitted then The response status is 403 and no authenticated session is returned\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee signs in successfully, the Folio3 Parking web app shall return a profile populated with corporate-directory employee details and administrator-maintained parking assignment, floor, and registered-vehicle records where present.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated employee has directory details and administrator-maintained assignment and vehicle records when The employee requests their profile then The response contains the employee ID, employee name, assigned parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle fields\",\n    \"Given An authenticated non-administrator requests another employee's profile when The profile request is submitted then The response status is 403\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If an active employee has no registered vehicle, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall require registration of at least one license plate before allowing that employee to use parking release or claim operations.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active employee has no registered vehicle when The employee submits a parking release or claim request then The response status is 409 and the error field identifies vehicle registration as required\",\n    \"Given An active employee submits a vehicle with a license plate and optional make, model, and color when The employee saves the vehicle profile then The response status is 201 and the returned vehicle record contains the plate and submitted optional fields\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"Where the caller has the Parking Administrator role, the Folio3 Parking web app shall allow that administrator to create, view, and update employee records, parking assignments, and registered-vehicle records.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The caller has the Parking Administrator role when The caller creates or updates an employee, assignment, or vehicle record then The response status is 200 or 201 and the returned record contains the submitted values\",\n    \"Given The caller does not have the Parking Administrator role when The caller submits an employee, assignment, or vehicle-record change then The response status is 403 and no record is changed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"Where the caller has the Parking Administrator role, the Folio3 Parking web app shall allow that administrator to configure the daily release time, per-floor space counts, work calendar, named report recipients, and administrator and Security Guard role assignments.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The caller has the Parking Administrator role when The caller saves release-time, floor-capacity, calendar, recipient, or role configuration then The response status is 200 and the returned configuration fields match the submitted values\",\n    \"Given The caller does not have the Parking Administrator role when The caller submits a configuration or role-assignment change then The response status is 403 and the configuration record is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking web app shall render every employee and administrator page as a responsive web page for phone, tablet, and desktop widths with touch-sized controls on narrow viewports.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A person opens each employee and administrator flow on phone, tablet, and desktop viewport sizes when The person navigates the flow and uses its primary controls then The screen shows the flow without horizontal page overflow and its primary controls can be operated by touch\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a dedicated parking holder submits today's release before that parking has been released or claimed, the Folio3 Parking web app shall record one release for that holder and date from a single user action.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The caller is a dedicated parking holder whose parking is reserved for today and not yet released or claimed when The caller submits a release request then The response status is 200 and exactly one release row exists for the holder and date\",\n    \"Given A dedicated holder opens today's parking screen with no existing release when The holder uses the release control once then The screen shows the parking status as Released\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While a dedicated assignment is expected to be used on a configured working day, the Folio3 Parking web app shall show Reserved by default and make a same-day release claimable at the configured daily release time if submitted earlier, or immediately if submitted later.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A dedicated holder submits a same-day release before the configured daily release time when The daily release time is reached in the Folio3 office time zone then The response from the availability request includes the released allocation and its status field is claimable\",\n    \"Given A dedicated holder submits a same-day release after the configured daily release time when An eligible employee requests availability then The response includes the released allocation immediately\",\n    \"Given A dedicated assignment has no release for the current working day when The holder requests parking status then The response status field is Reserved\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking web app shall accept a dedicated holder's release schedule for one or more dates no more than 30 days ahead and make each scheduled release claimable at the daily release time on its selected date.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A dedicated holder submits one or more selected dates within the next 30 days when The holder saves the schedule then The response status is 201 and the returned list contains a release record for each selected date\",\n    \"Given A dedicated holder submits a selected date more than 30 days ahead when The holder saves the schedule then The response status is 400 and no release row is created for that date\",\n    \"Given A holder has scheduled a release for a future date when The holder opens the release calendar then The screen shows the selected date and scheduled release status\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a scheduled release has not been claimed, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall allow its holder to cancel it; if it has been claimed, the app shall reject holder cancellation and preserve the claim.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A scheduled release has not been claimed when Its holder submits a cancellation then The response status is 200 and the release row has a cancelled status\",\n    \"Given A scheduled release has already been claimed when Its holder submits a cancellation then The response status is 409 and the claim row remains unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking web app shall expose claimable parking availability to active Folio3 employees who have no dedicated assignment and at least one registered vehicle, including the current available-space count.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active employee has no dedicated assignment and at least one registered vehicle when The employee requests parking availability then The response contains a count field and a list of claimable released allocations\",\n    \"Given An employee is inactive, has a dedicated assignment, or has no registered vehicle when The employee requests or attempts to claim availability then The response status is 403 or 409 and no claim row is created\",\n    \"Given An eligible employee opens the parking availability page when The page finishes loading then The screen displays the current number of available parking spaces\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When eligible employees claim released parking, the Folio3 Parking web app shall assign each release to only the earliest accepted claim and return the assigned floor from configured floor capacity.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Two eligible employees submit claims for the same last available release concurrently when The claims are processed then Exactly one response reports success, exactly one claim row exists, and the other response status is 409\",\n    \"Given An eligible employee claims a released allocation when The claim is accepted then The response contains the assigned floor field and one claim row records the employee, date, time, and allocation\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a temporary parking claim is confirmed, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall prevent the claimant from cancelling that claim.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An employee has a confirmed temporary parking claim when The employee submits a claim-cancellation request then The response status is 403 or 409 and the claim row remains confirmed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a released parking allocation becomes claimable, the Folio3 Parking web app shall send an email notification using a fixed template to eligible employees without dedicated parking who have a registered vehicle.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A released allocation becomes claimable and eligible employees have email addresses when The availability event is processed then An email message is sent to eligible employee addresses using the configured fixed template\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a permanently stickered vehicle arrives, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall leave its existing sticker process unaffected and preserve any temporary claim already made for that date, including when configured capacity is exceeded.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A temporary claim exists and a permanently stickered vehicle arrival is recorded when The arrival is processed then The temporary claim row remains valid and its authorization status is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the Folio3 LPR integration submits a detected car and readable plate, the Folio3 Parking web app shall verify the plate against that date's temporary parking authorizations and activate the green indicator only for a valid authorization.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The LPR integration submits a readable plate matching a valid temporary authorization for the current date when The entrance verification request is processed then The indicator integration receives an activation call and the response status is authorized\",\n    \"Given The LPR integration submits a readable plate with no valid temporary authorization when The entrance verification request is processed then The indicator receives no activation call and the response status is denied\",\n    \"Given The LPR integration submits a non-car detection when The entrance event is processed then No authorization response is returned and no indicator activation call is made\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If the LPR, plate-reading service, connection, or indicator cannot verify an authorization, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall leave the green indicator inactive and deny entry through the temporary-parking process.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An entrance verification encounters an unreadable plate or unavailable verification integration when The verification request is processed then The response status is denied and no green-indicator activation call is made\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking web app shall record every successful and unsuccessful entrance verification attempt with its timestamp, plate when readable, result, and entry status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An entrance verification succeeds or fails when The verification request is processed then One verification row records the timestamp, readable plate or empty plate field, result, and entry status\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking web app shall record daily utilization events using registered-vehicle entry records, counting an allocation as used when any vehicle registered to its employee is detected that day.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A dedicated holder has not released a parking allocation for a configured working day and one of the holder's registered plates has an entry record when The daily utilization job runs then The utilization row records the dedicated allocation as used\",\n    \"Given A dedicated holder has not released a parking allocation and none of the holder's registered plates has an entry record for a configured working day when The daily utilization job runs then The utilization row records Unused Dedicated Parking\",\n    \"Given An employee has a confirmed temporary claim and none of that employee's registered plates has an entry record for that day when The daily utilization job runs then The utilization row records Unused Temporary Parking with the employee, vehicle, and date fields\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the weekly reporting job runs on Monday morning in the Folio3 office time zone, the Folio3 Parking web app shall generate a report containing unused dedicated and temporary parking, daily and weekly utilization statistics, released-space and claim totals, and an overall utilization-percentage field.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The Monday-morning weekly reporting job runs with utilization and parking records available when The report is generated then The report file contains unused dedicated and temporary parking lists, daily and weekly statistics, released-space and claim counts, and an overall utilization-percentage field\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"Where a Parking Administrator has configured a named report-recipient list, the Folio3 Parking web app shall send weekly report emails only to addresses on that list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A named report-recipient list contains configured addresses and the weekly report job runs when The report email is sent then Email messages are sent to every configured recipient and no message is sent to any other address\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"Where a Parking Administrator views utilization records, the Folio3 Parking web app shall provide filterable on-screen lists and CSV export of the displayed records.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Parking Administrator opens utilization records when The administrator applies a filter and exports the displayed list then The screen shows records matching the filter and the downloaded file is a CSV containing those displayed records\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking web app shall retain parking-release audit history, LPR verification attempts, and utilization events according to Folio3's existing records-retention policy.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A release, verification attempt, or utilization event has been recorded and its retention period is governed by the Folio3 policy when The retention job processes the record then The record remains available until the policy's applicable retention period expires\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking web app shall limit Phase 1 utilization functionality to monitoring, recording, and reporting without applying automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An employee has an unused parking utilization record when The utilization job and weekly report job process that record then No warning, suspension, or penalty event or record is created\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"Responsive employee and administrator pages must remain usable across phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized primary controls.\",\n  \"The responsive web app must support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n  \"The system must support the first-year scale assumed for employee accounts and stored records.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}